# Interview Questions

## What is SSH Password-less Authentication?

A mechanism that uses SSH key pairs instead of passwords to authenticate users.

---

## Which File Stores Public Keys on the Server?

```text
~/.ssh/authorized_keys
```

---

## What is the Difference Between id_rsa and id_rsa.pub?

| File       | Purpose     |
| ---------- | ----------- |
| id_rsa     | Private Key |
| id_rsa.pub | Public Key  |

---

## What Does ssh-copy-id Do?

Copies the public key from the local machine to the remote server's authorized_keys file.

---

## Why Is Password-less SSH Important in DevOps?

Because automation tools such as Jenkins, Ansible, Terraform, backup scripts, and monitoring systems require non-interactive authentication.

